[Intro]

[Verse 1]
[00:33.26]She came from no village we knew of
[00:36.18]She came on no path we had walked
[00:39.09]Her staff was of ash, and her cloak was of crow
[00:42.69]And the snow did not bear her a track

[00:44.95]She asked for no bread and no bench at the fire
[00:48.02]She asked for no name we could give
[00:50.83]She asked but for nine of our oldest stones
[00:54.03]And the last of the salt we did keep

[Pre-Chorus]
[00:56.99]Seiðr, seiðr, seiðr
[00:59.97]Galdr, galdr, galdr

[Chorus]
[01:02.81]She set the nine stones in a ring on the ice!
[01:05.47]She drew the salt round in a stave!
[01:08.25]She bound her own hair to the head of her staff
[01:11.47]And she sang what the sun-mother gave!
[01:14.55]Galdr! Galdr Vǫlvunnar!
[01:17.41]She singeth what none dareth sing!
[01:20.13]She traded the breath in her body away
[01:23.20]For the sun and the green and the spring!

[Verse 2]
[01:37.76]She spake of the white wolf that swalloweth dawn
[01:40.65]She spake of the worm 'neath the world
[01:43.53]She spake of the door that the gods had shut fast
[01:46.52]And the key that the deep wood had hurled

[01:49.36]She named what the priests could not name in their books
[01:52.21]She named what the smiths could not forge
[01:55.25]She sang in a tongue that was older than tongues
[01:58.28]And the ice on the river did groan

[Pre-Chorus]
[02:01.33]Seiðr, seiðr, seiðr
[02:04.34]Galdr, galdr, galdr

[Chorus]
[02:07.11]She set the nine stones in a ring on the ice!
[02:09.81]She drew the salt round in a stave!
[02:12.66]She bound her own hair to the head of her staff
[02:15.32]And she sang what the sun-mother gave!
[02:18.91]Galdr! Galdr Vǫlvunnar!
[02:21.59]She singeth what none dareth sing!
[02:24.39]She traded the breath in her body away
[02:27.36]For the sun and the green and the spring!

[Bridge]
[02:30.55]And the wood did hear, where it had not heard
[02:33.32]And the moss beneath the snow did stir
[02:36.29]And a green thing wakened in the root of the ash
[02:39.09]And the white wolf's jaw did unclench, and unclench

[02:42.01]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir
[02:48.42]Heyr oss now
[02:50.97]She is paying with her marrow
[02:53.85]She is paying with her brow

[Breakdown]
[02:57.03]Nine the stones!
[02:58.46]Nine the names!
[02:59.90]Nine the strides she did not return!
[03:02.82]Nine the songs!
[03:04.11]Nine the wounds!
[03:05.73]Nine the candles we did burn!

[Final Chorus]
[03:43.55]She set the nine stones in a ring on the ice!
[03:46.67]She drew the salt round in a stave!
[03:49.41]She bound her own hair to the head of her staff
[03:52.38]And she sang what the sun-mother gave!
[03:55.49]Galdr! Galdr Vǫlvunnar!
[03:58.22]She singeth what none dareth sing!
[04:01.07]She traded the breath in her body away
[04:04.03]For the sun and the green and the spring!

[Outro]
[04:07.39]Vár... vár... vár kemr...
